    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The term 'armed rebellion' replaced 'internal disturbance' as a ground for National Emergency through the 44th Amendment Act, 1978.",
        "Fundamental Rights guaranteed under Articles 20 and 21 cannot be suspended even during a National Emergency.",
        "A proclamation of National Emergency must be approved by both Houses of Parliament within 1 month by a special majority.",
        "Financial Emergency under Article 360 has never been declared in India."
      ],
      "id": "dn1kl7h"
